-3|0@hardware^1440701590#cuhrksr:rdfox$:I read it and I work in the industry and it's utter bullshit. Samsung Semiconductor is a US company owned by a Korean company. They are not particularly shady by US standards. A few years ago Rambus won a patent infringement settlement against them for $900 million dollars. Most of us think Rambus is a patent troll, but there's two sides to every story. Suffice it say Samy will be keeping his nose clean for the foreseeable future. TSMC says Samsung's product looks similar which it should. Neither company develops their process. They are primarily operations companies who buy all their processes and equipment from companies like Applied Materials. Maybe a long time ago when things were simpler, fabs developed their own processes but now it's done collaboratively according to an industry roadmap. Basically, if you bake the same dough in the same oven, the cookies are going to taste the same. Anyway, there's no one guy who can push technology forward by his mere presence. Especially this Liang guy who is middle-management. Liang could help Samy get an unfair advantage by disclosing some high-level financial information if he had access to it. But everyone knows that is illegal and he would not last a day at his new job if he walked in the door with competitor's internal documents.
