1|0@hardware^1440727244#cui6raq:PVonMuter$:You're absolutely right, when it comes to business against other countries Japan, China, and Korea see themselves as wholes rather than many businesses. They'll work together against foreigners, which no western business that I know of will do. Also, you're correct in calling them huge corporations in a sense. Korea and Japan were organized under Keynesian economics, so government control of economy was far larger from the get go, rather than America which is slowly becoming more Keynesian. It would make sense under Keynesian views that the government providing espionage for the "good of the economy" would be accepted. Of course that's all self speculation.
